        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "75983eff-3ecb-52fe-89a1-19d3d51f49c8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: R Adams Cowley, Dwight D. Eisenhower\n- Roles: surgeon, emergency medicine pioneer, President of the United States, Army general\n- Concepts: trauma medicine, shock trauma, open-heart surgery, pacemaker\n\nFacts:\n- Dwight D. Eisenhower was an American politician and Army general who served as the 34th President of the United States from 1953 to 1961.\n- R Adams Cowley was born on July 25, 1917, and died on October 27, 1991.\n- R Adams Cowley was an American surgeon known as the \"Father of Trauma Medicine\" and was considered a pioneer in emergency medicine and the treatment of shock trauma.\n- R Adams Cowley was one of the first surgeons to perform open-heart surgery.\n- R Adams Cowley invented a surgical clamp that bears his name.\n- R Adams Cowley invented a prototype pacemaker that was used by Dwight D. Eisenhower.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "cbbb34a3-a02f-5df5-81c9-45f653de8161",
        "text": "Page: R Adams Cowley. Sentence: R Adams Cowley (July 25, 1917 – October 27, 1991), the \"Father of Trauma Medicine,\" was an American surgeon considered a pioneer in emergency medicine and the treatment of shock trauma.\nPage: R Adams Cowley. Sentence: He is also known for being one of the first surgeons to perform open-heart surgery and invented both a surgical clamp that bears his name and a prototype pacemaker that was used by Dwight D. Eisenhower.\nPage: Dwight D. Eisenhower. Sentence: Dwight David \"Ike\" Eisenhower ( ; October 14, 1890 – March 28, 1969) was an American politician and Army general who served as the 34th President of the United States from 1953 until 1961.",
